cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these replication materials, please cite the paper."
title: >-
  Replication materials — Climate misinformation and quoted liquidity in energy equities
abstract: >-
  Replication code, fixed classification scores, input audits and submission
  materials for a study of climate content and quoted liquidity in energy
  equities. The principal model uses 485800 security-days on 202 securities,
  market-day and sector-month fixed effects, prior-session controls and
  sector/date inference. The daily content index is built from fixed
  classifications of 217954 English-language Facebook posts.
authors:
  - family-names: Rice
    given-names: James K.
    affiliation: University of Essex
version: "3.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-23"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - climate misinformation
  - information asymmetry
  - market microstructure
  - bid-ask spread
  - large language models
  - replication package
